  "summary_markdown": "## Postmortem: CoD-fidelity browser FPS (run 34092038605, issue #58)\n\n### Outcome\nShipped STRIKE PROTOCOL, a zero-dependency single-file raycaster FPS (~49KB index.html + game/index.html), verified in real headless Chrome against both localhost:3000 and the public Cloudflare tunnel (title, deploy, combat, pause, win/fail, persistence all green, zero page errors), with 8 final-* screenshots, branch opencode/34092038605 pushed (e04c111), and completion evidence posted to issue #58. Workflow steps report success except Delivery (not yet run).\n\n### What worked\n- 7 high-signal CoD anchors recorded with URLs+purpose in PROGRESS.md and mapped to concrete HUD/loop decisions.\n- Real-browser verification loop (puppeteer-core + installed Chrome) was the highest-value activity: screenshots plus state assertions (kills, HP, mode, XP across reload) proved the full gameplay loop.\n- Fresh-context critic subagent produced a ranked 5-gap list; the top gap (touch Mission-2 soft-lock) got fixed.\n- Build-then-verify discipline: node vm syntax checks gated every edit; PROGRESS.md stayed resumable throughout.\n\n### What did not work\n- Syntax-only verification gave false confidence: two load/frame-time runtime crashes (null-weapons TypeError killing all logic; minimap TDZ ReferenceError blanking minimap+compass every frame) survived syntax checks and an earlier premature [goal:complete]. Only real-browser execution caught them.\n- Sandbox blocks CLI loopback TCP: curl/python Champion retries against 127.0.0.1:8931/3000 timed out repeatedly (wasted turns, a 120s shell timeout, a stale python server left running) before discovering Chrome's networking was unaffected.\n- app.log shows the harness tried `npm` with no package.json (ENOENT) — the static single-file design has no start script, so workflow app-launch assumptions mismatched the artifact.\n- Two prior [goal:complete] claims were rejected for missing evidence format before the final accepted one.\n- Quality-bar items only partially honored: no blind A/B vs anchors, touch verified via emulation only (one synthetic touchstart), ~23fps measured only under software rendering, enemies remain unanimated billboards.\n- Workflow-evidence file snapshot shows game sources untracked at capture time; commit/push happened later in-session, so evidence timing understates final delivery state.\n\n### Root causes\n- No testable-runtime gate before claiming done: static checks cannot catch TDZ/null-at-load faults in browser-only globals.\n- Environment networking asymmetry (CLI loopback blocked, browser OK) was undocumented; the agent retried the failing path instead of switching transports sooner.\n- Artifact shape (single static HTML) vs harness expectation (npm app) was never reconciled up front.\n- Completion-format rejections consumed turns that a checklist or template would have prevented.\n\n### Prioritized improvements\n1. Require a real-browser smoke test (console-error-free load + one gameplay transition + screenshot) before any completion claim on browser deliverables.\n2. On first loopback failure, switch to browser-transport verification immediately; document sandbox networking limits in the session notes.\n3. Declare artifact shape early (static vs npm) and align the serve/launch path with the harness.\n4. Keep completion-format requirements as a copy-paste template in the goal notes to avoid rejected submissions.\n5. Close fidelity gaps explicitly (enemy animation, spawn yaw, GPU fps measurement) or record them as accepted limitations before claiming the quality bar is met.",
